SUMMARY:Dec 8 - How to Let Long-tail Guide Your 3D Annotation Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Raleigh AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\nJoin
  us on Dec 8 for the “How to Let Long-tail Guide Your 3D Annotation” w
 orkshop with [Eric Hofesmann](https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-hofesmann/)
 .\n\n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nDec 08\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 10:00 AM PST
 \nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/how-to-let
 -long-tail-guide-your-3d-annotation-december-8-2026)**\n\nAutonomous drivi
 ng models rarely fail on the common case. They fail on the long-tail: the 
 pedestrian stepping out from behind a parked truck or a construction zone 
 that matches nothing in the training set. Each of those moments lives in s
 ynchronized multi-sensor data\, made up of a LiDAR sweep\, a ring of camer
 as\, a timestamp\, and a calibration. Fixing one means finding it\, labeli
 ng it in 3D\, and proving the next model handles it.\n\nIn this live sessi
 on\, we will take long-tail driving scenarios from discovery to 3D labels 
 to evaluation\, and make the case that 3D ground truth should be built whe
 re your data lives\, not exported away from it.
